    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25959" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕrālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		2. latus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the side,
				lateral</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj. (ante- and post-class.): lateralis dolor, Enn. ap.
			Victor. p. 1963 P. (Ann. v. 601 Vahl.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for which: lateris dolor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 21, 89, § 155</span></i>
			): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cingula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 6, 40</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lătĕrālĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>saddle-bags</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 32, 1, 102</span></i>.</div>
